invariant: INV-16
file: widemul.h
catches: widemul_runtime_test
reason: widemul_rsa_pss_sign_key_ok inverts its branch, so a session that
  does not state its multiply runs rsa_sign64_key_ok, which multiplies the
  key's primes on the native multiply, and a session that states it runs
  the test that reads no prime. Every key a test provisions is well
  formed, so both tests admit it and nothing else notices.
  bin/widemul_runtime_test counts the calls into the 64-bit signer's test
  and requires one under the constant-time answer and none under any
  other.

--- old
    if (widemul_native(widemul)) {
        return rsa_sign64_key_ok(k);
--- new
    if (!widemul_native(widemul)) {
        return rsa_sign64_key_ok(k);
